patches.behavior:
State per loop index: `{ position: [x, y], velocity: [vx, vy], dragging: false, coasting: false, touched: false, grab: [x, y], ignoreUntilRelease: false, initialized: false }`.

Each frame:
```
const start = ctx.input("startPosition");
const lo = [Math.min(min[0], max[0]), Math.min(min[1], max[1])];
const hi = [Math.max(min[0], max[0]), Math.max(min[1], max[1])];
const limit = (p) => clip ? [clamp(p[0], lo[0], hi[0]), clamp(p[1], lo[1], hi[1])] : p;
const mask = axis === "horizontal" ? [1, 0] : axis === "vertical" ? [0, 1] : [1, 1];
const p = ctx.services.pointer(layerRef);            // layerRef null = whole screen
if (!state.initialized) { state.position = limit(start); state.initialized = true; }

if (ctx.pulsed("reset")) {
  state.position = limit(start); state.velocity = [0, 0];
  state.dragging = false; state.coasting = false; state.touched = false;
  state.ignoreUntilRelease = p.down;
} else if (!enabled) {
  if (state.dragging) state.ignoreUntilRelease = p.down;
  state.dragging = false; state.coasting = false; state.velocity = [0, 0];
} else {
  if (!state.touched) state.position = limit(start);
  if (!state.dragging && p.began && !state.ignoreUntilRelease) {
    state.dragging = true; state.coasting = false; state.touched = true;
    state.grab = state.position;                        // catches a coasting layer
  }
  if (state.dragging) {
    const t = toParentSpace(p.translation);
    state.position = limit([state.grab[0] + t[0] * mask[0], state.grab[1] + t[1] * mask[1]]);
    const v = toParentSpace(p.velocity);
    state.velocity = [v[0] * mask[0], v[1] * mask[1]];
    if (p.ended) {
      state.dragging = false;
      if (momentum && Math.hypot(...state.velocity) > 0.25) state.coasting = true;
      else state.velocity = [0, 0];
    }
  } else if (state.coasting) {
    coastPerAxis(ctx.dt);                              // see Momentum below
    ctx.requestNextFrame();
  }
}
if (!p.down) state.ignoreUntilRelease = false;
ctx.output("position", state.position);
ctx.output("dragging", state.dragging);
ctx.output("velocity", state.velocity);
```

- Gesture source: `ctx.services.pointer({ layerId, instance })`. A drag starts on the frame a press begins on the layer or one of its descendants (touches bubble, ARCHITECTURE.md §5.5); there is no slop, so the layer moves from the first point of movement. Only the first pointer that pressed drives the drag; extra fingers are ignored until it lifts.
- Parent space: `toParentSpace` divides pointer deltas by the product of the ancestor scales from `ctx.services.layerInfo` (previous frame). Rotated ancestors aren't compensated in v1.
- Momentum: deceleration per millisecond `d = 1 − max(momentumFriction, 1) / 25000` (50 → 0.998 normal, 250 → 0.99 fast, 950 → 0.962). Per axis: `kv = d^(1000·dt)`, `x += (v / 1000) · d · (1 − kv) / (1 − d)`, `v *= kv` (POP decay, gap-fill §4.2.4). Coasting ends when the speed drops below 0.25 pt/s. With Clip on, an axis that reaches a bound stops there and its velocity becomes 0 (hard stop, no bounce).
- Pulses: `reset` is the only pulse. It wins over a press in the same frame, and the current touch can't restart a drag until it lifts. Pulses on consecutive frames each reset.
- Frame 0: Position is `limit(startPosition)`, Dragging false, Velocity `[0, 0]`. No drag can start on frame 0 because hit tests use the previous frame's layout.
- Start Position: followed live until the first drag after a restart or Reset; later changes apply on the next Reset.
- Retargeting: changing Clip, Min, Max, or Axis applies on the next frame, re-clamping Position (including mid-drag and mid-coast).
- Loops: per-index state. A looped Layer gives each index its own pointer target (`instance` = loop index), so every replicated layer drags independently. New indices start at their Start Position; removed indices drop their state.
- Edge cases: `min > max` on an axis is swapped per axis. `min == max` on an axis locks that axis when Clip is on. A missing or deleted layer never receives presses, so Position holds. Non-finite inputs are treated as 0 with one warning per restart through `ctx.services.log("warn", …)`.
- Disabled: new presses are ignored, an active drag ends with no momentum (the touch must lift before it can drag again), coasting stops where it is, and Position holds.
- Muted: Position outputs Start Position, Dragging false, Velocity `[0, 0]`.
- Evaluation: `alwaysEvaluate`; call `ctx.requestNextFrame()` while dragging or coasting.
- Restart and dispose: state resets to Start Position. Nothing to release.
- Coming from Origami: Drag Settings folds in as advanced inputs; importers move a linked Drag Settings patch's literals onto these ports. Momentum Friction's mapping is a Sonobe decision (no published formula).

State per loop index: one axis record per axis `{ offset: 0, velocity: 0, phase: "idle" | "tracking" | "decelerating" | "rubberBanding" | "snapping", spring, rawGrab, startPage, lastWheelTime }` plus `{ touch: "none" | "pending" | "accepted" | "ignored", slopOrigin: [x, y], lock: null | "x" | "y" }`.

Geometry, per axis `a`, recomputed every frame from the previous frame's layout (`ctx.services.layerInfo`):
```
info = layerInfo(layerRef); parent = info.parent ? layerInfo(parentRef) : null;
viewport = parent ? parent.size[a] : device().screenSize[a];
content  = contentSize[a] > 0 ? contentSize[a] : info.size[a];
topLeft  = startPosition[a] − info.anchor[a] · info.size[a];   // content's top-left at offset 0
Free:   hi = 0; lo = min(0, viewport − (topLeft + content));
Paging: page = pageSize[a] > 0 ? pageSize[a] : viewport; step = page + pagePadding[a];
        inset = (viewport − page) / 2; count = max(1, round((content + pagePadding[a]) / step));
        pageOffset(n) = inset − topLeft − n · step; lo = pageOffset(count − 1); hi = pageOffset(0);
Off:    lo = hi = 0 (the axis never moves).
```

Each frame:
```
p = ctx.services.pointer(layerRef);
1. Jumps (checked first; they work even while disabled):
   if (ctx.pulsed("jumpToX")) jump(x, jumpPositionX − startPosition[0], jumpStyleX);
   if (ctx.pulsed("jumpToY")) jump(y, jumpPositionY − startPosition[1], jumpStyleY);
   jump(axis, target, style): target = clamp(target, lo, hi); cancel an active touch (touch = "ignored");
     instant → offset = target, velocity = 0, phase idle; animated → snap spring from offset keeping velocity.
2. Touch (when enabled):
   p.began → touch = "pending"; slopOrigin = p.position; every moving axis stops where it is
             (a tap catches a fling); rawGrab = inverseRubberBandClamp(offset, lo, hi, viewport, 0.55).
   pending and distance(p.position, p.startPosition) > 10 → decide:
     d = p.position − p.startPosition; dominant = |d.x| > |d.y| ? "x" : "y";
     if directionLocking and both axes are on → lock = dominant;
     if directionLocking and only one axis is on and dominant is the other → touch = "ignored";
     else touch = "accepted"; slopOrigin = p.position (no 10 pt jump).
   accepted and p.down → for each active axis (lock ? only lock : every non-Off axis):
     raw = rawGrab + (p.position[a] − slopOrigin[a]) / ancestorScale[a];
     offset = rubberBand ? rubberBandClamp(raw, lo, hi, viewport, 0.55) : clamp(raw, lo, hi); phase tracking.
   p.ended and accepted → release(a, p.velocity[a] / ancestorScale[a]) for each active axis; touch = "none".
   p.ended otherwise → touch = "none" (a tap or ignored touch leaves the content resting).
3. Wheel (enabled, no accepted touch, ctx.services.pointer(parentRef).hovering):
   w = ctx.services.wheel().delta; for each non-Off axis: offset = clamp(offset − w[a], lo, hi); phase idle;
   lastWheelTime = ctx.time. A Paging axis snaps to its nearest page once 0.15 s pass with no wheel delta.
4. Step every axis not tracking by ctx.dt (capped at 0.064 s): see Physics.
5. position = [startPosition[0] + offset.x, startPosition[1] + offset.y];
   ctx.output("position", position); ctx.output("x", position[0]); ctx.output("y", position[1]);
   ctx.output("pageX", pageIndex(x)); ctx.output("pageY", pageIndex(y));
   ctx.output("dragging", touch === "accepted"); ctx.output("moving", any axis phase !== "idle");
```

- Physics (the Momentum Scrolling primitive, gap-fill R8; `MomentumScroller` in `@sonobe/engine`):
  - `release(a, v)`, Free axis: outside `[lo, hi]` → rubber-band spring to the nearest bound with velocity `v`. Otherwise, if `|v| > 0.25` → decelerate with POP decay `d` = 0.998 per ms (Normal) or 0.99 (Fast): `kv = d^(1000·dt)`, `offset += (v/1000)·d·(1 − kv)/(1 − d)`, `v *= kv`, idle below 0.25 pt/s. Otherwise idle.
  - Crossing a bound while decelerating: with Rubber Band on, a spring starts at the bound with the remaining velocity (sub-frame exact via the decay closed form); with it off, the axis stops at the bound.
  - Rubber-band spring: Origami tension 40, friction 10 through `fromOrigamiTensionFriction`, mass 1, RK4 at 1 ms substeps, rest threshold 0.001.
  - `release(a, v)`, Paging axis: `projected = offset + v · 0.99 / (1 − 0.99) / 1000`; `n = round((hi − projected) / step)`, clamped to `startPage ± 1` and `[0, count − 1]`; snap spring (bounciness 0, speed 12 through `fromBouncinessSpeed`) to `pageOffset(n)` with velocity `v`. A drag that overshoots backward can't land on a page past its start page.
  - Idle and out of bounds (content shrank, or a jump target moved): spring back to the nearest bound, or clamp when Rubber Band is off.
- Page index: Paging axis → `clamp(round((hi − offset) / step), 0, count − 1)`. Free or Off axis → `clamp(round(−offset / pageSizeOrViewport), 0, ∞)`, so it still counts screens.
- Pulses: `jumpToX` and `jumpToY`. Same-frame precedence: jump > touch > wheel. Pulses on consecutive frames each jump.
- Frame 0: offsets are 0, Position = Start Position, pages 0, Dragging and Moving false. Layout sizes arrive from frame 1 (layer-derived values lag one frame, gap-fill R2), so bounds are recomputed then.
- Nested scrolls: a touch bubbles to every Scroll whose content contains it. With Direction Locking on, a one-axis Scroll ignores touches that start in the other direction, which lets a horizontal carousel sit inside a vertical feed. Two Scrolls on the same axis both move in v1; exclusive claiming needs an engine-level pointer claim.
- Retargeting: changing Scroll X/Y, sizes, padding, or Start Position recomputes the bounds on the next frame and springs the content back into range. Changing Deceleration Rate affects the next release.
- Loops: per-index state. A looped Layer scrolls each replicated layer independently (`instance` = loop index).
- Edge cases: content smaller than the viewport → `lo = hi = 0`, but it still rubber-bands while dragged when Rubber Band is on. A missing layer or missing layout → content size 0 and no presses. Negative sizes are treated as 0. `step ≤ 0` (Page Size and padding both 0 with no viewport) → paging falls back to Free for that axis and warns once. Non-finite inputs are treated as 0 with one warning per restart.
- Disabled: touches and wheel are ignored; an active drag releases with zero velocity (overscroll still springs back); decelerating axes stop where they are; jumps still apply; Position holds.
- Muted: Position outputs Start Position, X and Y its components, pages 0, Dragging and Moving false.
- Evaluation: `alwaysEvaluate`; call `ctx.requestNextFrame()` while any axis isn't idle.
- Restart and dispose: offsets reset to 0. Nothing to release.
- Coming from Origami: Scroll Settings folds in as advanced inputs; importers move a linked Scroll Settings patch's literals here. Origami outputs a content offset for Position X/Y fields; Sonobe outputs a whole Position (Start Position + offset).

State: `{ position: [0, 0] }` (a single global instance; no per-index differences).

Each frame:
```
const p = ctx.services.pointer(null);        // whole screen
if (p.down || p.hovering || p.ended) state.position = p.position;
const w = ctx.services.wheel();
ctx.output("position", state.position);
ctx.output("left", buttonHeld(p, 0));
ctx.output("right", buttonHeld(p, 2));
ctx.output("middle", buttonHeld(p, 1));
ctx.output("scrollDelta", w.delta);
ctx.output("scrollVelocity", ctx.dt > 0 ? [w.delta[0] / ctx.dt, w.delta[1] / ctx.dt] : [0, 0]);
```

- Position: the last known pointer position in prototype coordinates. It updates on moves with or without a pressed button, holds when the pointer leaves the viewer, and is `[0, 0]` before the first pointer event.
- Buttons: DOM button numbers, 0 left, 1 middle, 2 right. A button is held from its `down` event until its `up` or `cancel`. Touch and pen presses count as Left. Contract gap: `PointerSnapshot` doesn't expose which buttons are held. Until it does (proposed: `buttons: number`, the DOM bitmask), `buttonHeld(p, 0)` is `p.down` for any button and Right and Middle stay false.
- Wheel: `ctx.services.wheel().delta` sums this frame's wheel events in points, positive y toward the bottom of a page (DOM `deltaY`). The renderer converts line and page deltas to points and applies the OS natural-scrolling setting. Trackpad momentum arrives as wheel events, so it shows up here. Scroll Velocity is `delta / dt`, so it matches at 60 and 120 fps; frames with no wheel events output `[0, 0]`.
- Frame 0: Position `[0, 0]` unless a pointer event arrives on frame 0; buttons false; scroll outputs `[0, 0]`.
- Loops: the patch has no inputs, so it never loops.
- Edge cases: several pointers pressed at once (multi-touch) report the first pressed pointer's position. Non-finite event coordinates are ignored.
- Platform and simulation: phones and tablets have no hover, right or middle button, or wheel; those outputs stay idle. In headless simulation, `pointer` and `wheel` InputEvents drive the outputs deterministically.
- Evaluation: `alwaysEvaluate` (the outputs change with input events, not inputs).
- Restart and dispose: Position resets to `[0, 0]`. Nothing to release.
- Coming from Origami: the per-frame Scroll Velocity becomes per second; Origami's legacy wheel patch flipped the y sign, Sonobe uses the DOM sign.

State per loop index: `{ on: false, spring: { value, velocity }, target, dragging: false, grab: 0, grabDistance: 0, grabAngle: 0, grabCentroid: [0, 0], trackedVelocity: 0, ignoreUntilRelease: false, initialized: false }`.

Each frame:
```
const lo = Math.min(start, end), hi = Math.max(start, end), span = Math.max(hi - lo, 1);
const config = fromBouncinessSpeed(bounciness, Math.max(speed, 0));   // BouncyConversion → k, c, mass 1
if (!state.initialized) { state.spring = { value: start, velocity: 0 }; state.initialized = true; }
const p = ctx.services.pointer(layerRef);

// 1. Pulses. Precedence: turnOff > turnOn > flip.
if (ctx.pulsed("turnOff")) { if (state.on) { state.on = false; cancelDrag(); } }
else if (ctx.pulsed("turnOn")) { if (!state.on) { state.on = true; cancelDrag(); } }
else if (ctx.pulsed("flip")) { state.on = !state.on; cancelDrag(); }

// 2. Gesture.
if (enabled && gesture !== "none" && !state.ignoreUntilRelease) {
  if (!state.dragging && gestureBegan(p)) { state.dragging = true; state.grab = state.spring.value; state.spring.velocity = 0; }
  if (state.dragging && gestureActive(p)) {
    const raw = gestureValue(state.grab);              // see Gestures
    state.spring.value = rubberBandClamp(raw, lo, hi, span, 0.55);
    state.spring.velocity = gestureVelocity();          // units per second
  } else if (state.dragging) release();
} else if (state.dragging) release();                  // disabled or gesture set to none mid-drag
if (!p.down) state.ignoreUntilRelease = false;

// 3. Animate toward the committed state.
state.target = state.on ? end : start;
if (!state.dragging) { stepSpring(state.spring, state.target, config, ctx.dt); ctx.requestNextFrame(); }

const progress = end !== start ? (state.spring.value - start) / (end - start) : (state.spring.value >= start ? 1 : 0);
ctx.output("output", state.spring.value); ctx.output("progress", progress);
ctx.output("on", state.on); ctx.output("dragging", state.dragging);
```

- `release()`: `projected = value + velocity · 0.099` (where a fast POP decay, 0.99 per ms, would come to rest). `on = |projected − end| < |projected − start|`; on a tie the state doesn't change. Then `dragging = false` and the spring starts from the current value with the release velocity.
- `cancelDrag()`: a pulse during a drag ends it. The spring keeps the tracked velocity, and the touch can't grab again until it lifts (`ignoreUntilRelease = p.down`).
- Gestures:
  - `swipeX` / `swipeY`: begins when a press begins on the layer (`p.began`), active while `p.down`. `gestureValue = grab + p.translation[a] / ancestorScale[a]`; velocity is `p.velocity[a] / ancestorScale[a]`. There's no slop: Value follows from the first movement.
  - `pinchScale`, `pinchRotate`, `pinchX`, `pinchY`: begin when a second finger presses on the layer and stay active while two fingers are down; lifting to one finger releases. With the two fingers' distance `dist`, angle `ang` (degrees, unwrapped so crossing ±180 doesn't jump), and centroid `c` captured at the start: Pinch Scale → `grab · dist / max(grabDistance, 1)`; Pinch Rotate → `grab + (ang − grabAngle)`; Pinch X / Pinch Y → `grab + (c[a] − grabCentroid[a])`. Velocity is an exponential moving average of the value's change per second (time constant 0.03 s), with no sample on the first pinch frame.
  - Contract gap: pinch needs every pointer's position, but `PointerSnapshot` exposes only the first plus `pointerCount`. Proposed: `RuntimeServices.pointers(layer)` (see Touches). Until then, pinch gestures never begin.
- Spring: RK4 at 1 ms substeps, `dt` capped at 0.064 s, rest threshold 0.001 on displacement and velocity, then snap to the target (semantics.md §7.5). Bounciness and Speed update the constants live without resetting motion.
- Pulses: `flip`, `turnOn`, `turnOff` with the precedence above. Turn On while already on and Turn Off while already off do nothing, even mid-drag. Pulses on consecutive frames each count. Pulses work while disabled and with Gesture None.
- Frame 0: Output = Start at rest, Progress 0, On false, Dragging false. A pulse on frame 0 applies on frame 0 and animates.
- Retargeting: changing Start or End moves the target; the spring keeps its velocity (C¹ continuous). While dragging, the rubber-band bounds update on the next frame.
- Loops: per-index state. A looped Layer gives each index its own gesture target (`instance` = loop index); looped Start, End, or pulses apply per index. New indices start at their Start, off.
- Edge cases: `start == end` → Progress is a step (1 when Output ≥ Start, else 0) and every release lands on that value. Negative Speed is treated as 0, and negative Bounciness adds damping, as in Pop Animation. A missing layer never begins a gesture. Non-finite inputs are treated as 0 with one warning per restart.
- Disabled: gestures are ignored and an active drag releases as if the fingers lifted; pulses and the spring keep working.
- Muted: Output = Start, Progress 0, On false, Dragging false.
- Evaluation: `alwaysEvaluate`; call `ctx.requestNextFrame()` while dragging or while the spring isn't at rest.
- Restart and dispose: state resets to off at Start. Nothing to release.
- Coming from Origami: Origami's docs say On/Off follows whichever value is closer during the gesture; Sonobe commits On at release (with flick projection) so downstream logic doesn't flicker mid-drag.

State per loop index: `{ output: 0, velocity: 0, phase: "idle" | "tracking" | "decelerating" | "rubberBanding", spring, lastValue: 0, initialized: false }`.

Each frame:
```
const lo = Math.min(startBoundary, endBoundary), hi = Math.max(startBoundary, endBoundary);
const d = 1 - clamp(scrollingFriction, 1, 100) / 2000;                  // per ms: 4 → 0.998, 20 → 0.99, 100 → 0.95
const rb = fromOrigamiTensionFriction(Math.max(rubberBandTension, 10), Math.max(rubberBandFriction, 10));
const target = stickToBoundaries ? clamp(value, lo, hi) : value;
const h = Math.min(Math.max(ctx.dt, 0), 0.064);
if (!state.initialized) { state.output = clamp(value, lo, hi); state.lastValue = state.output; state.initialized = true; }

if (tracking) {
  if (state.phase !== "tracking") { state.velocity = 0; state.lastValue = target; state.phase = "tracking"; }
  else if (h > 0) {
    const sample = (target - state.lastValue) / h;
    state.velocity += (sample - state.velocity) * (1 - Math.exp(-h / 0.03));
    state.lastValue = target;
  }
  state.output = target;
} else {
  if (state.phase === "tracking") release(state.velocity);
  step(h);
}
ctx.output("output", state.output);
ctx.output("velocity", state.phase === "idle" ? 0 : state.velocity);
ctx.output("moving", state.phase === "decelerating" || state.phase === "rubberBanding");
```

- `release(v)`: outside `[lo, hi]` → phase rubberBanding (spring toward the nearest bound, starting with velocity `v`; with Stick to Boundaries on, clamp and go idle instead). Otherwise `|v| > 0.25` → phase decelerating. Otherwise idle with velocity 0.
- `step(h)`, decelerating: POP decay (gap-fill §4.2.4): `kv = d^(1000·h)`, `output += (v/1000)·d·(1 − kv)/(1 − d)`, `v *= kv`. If the path crosses a bound within this frame, find the crossing time from the closed form. With Stick to Boundaries, stop at the bound (velocity 0, idle). Without it, start the rubber-band spring at the bound with the remaining velocity `v·d^(1000·t)` and integrate the rest of the frame. Below 0.25 units/s → idle.
- `step(h)`, rubberBanding: RK4 at 1 ms substeps with k and c from `rb`, mass 1 (semantics.md §7.5); at rest (0.001 on displacement and velocity) → output = the bound, velocity 0, idle.
- `step(h)`, idle: if the bounds moved so Output is now outside them, spring back (or clamp with Stick to Boundaries).
- Tracking velocity: an exponential moving average of Value's change per second (time constant 0.03 s). The first tracking frame takes no sample, so grabbing while coasting doesn't spike. Grabbing catches any motion in flight immediately.
- Value while not tracking: ignored. To reposition Output programmatically, turn Tracking on for a frame with the new Value.
- Pulses: none. Tracking is a state; a pulse wired into it tracks for exactly one frame and then releases with velocity 0 (a one-frame sample).
- Frame 0: Output = Value clamped to the boundaries, Velocity 0, Moving false. If Tracking is on at frame 0, Output = Value.
- Retargeting: new boundaries apply on the next frame; a coasting Output that's now out of range springs back. Friction, tension, and Stick to Boundaries changes apply immediately without resetting motion.
- Loops: per-index state; every index coasts independently. New indices start at their Value; removed indices drop their state.
- Edge cases: `startBoundary > endBoundary` is swapped. Equal boundaries pin Output to that value after release. Scrolling Friction outside 1–100 and rubber-band values below 10 are clamped for the physics (not rewritten). Non-finite Value or boundaries are treated as 0 with one warning per restart.
- Muted: Output passes Value through, Velocity 0, Moving false.
- Evaluation: `alwaysEvaluate`; call `ctx.requestNextFrame()` while decelerating or rubber-banding.
- Restart and dispose: state resets on restart. Nothing to release.
- Coming from Origami: Origami starts Output at the End Boundary on the first frame (default 99999), which its sample files work around; Sonobe starts at Value. Scrolling Friction's mapping to deceleration is a Sonobe decision anchored so the legacy default 4 equals POP's 0.998 per ms. Rubber band values use Origami's tension and friction units.
